<title>BELGIUM: EU farmers see higher 1997 wheat harvest.</title>
<headline>EU farmers see higher 1997 wheat harvest.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A further boost to EU wheat production is likely in the 1997 harvest, an official of the federation of European Union farmers' groups (COPA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>While autumn plantings of winter wheat were impeded by weather it is likely that this will be compensated by increased spring plantings, Peter Myllerup said.</p>
<p>The reduction in set-aside in the 1996/97 (July/June) crop year from 10 percent to five percent of total arable area can be expected to be concentrated in grains and particularly in wheat</p>
</text>
